{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts","id":954094,"title":"Taking Out-of-Tribe Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-19T16:35:02-07:00","id":954094,"title":"Taking Out-of-Tribe Gifts","content":"A common house rule (I'm assuming it's an house rule?) I've seen in games I've played is a loss of temporary renown for taking gifts that are outside your tribe, breed, or auspice. For those of you who use this rule, what's your reasoning behind it?<br /> '<br /> I can see the logic in some NPCs looking down on those who step outside their 'roles' (say, an Ahroun learning Command Spirit), but why would it be discouraged to learn something like Mother's Touch, which could mean the difference between life and death in a fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11550-cinnabar","name":"Cinnabar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:16:50-07:00","id":954113,"title":"","content":"It's kind of on the border of &quot;house rule,&quot; and &quot;loose application&quot; of the rules. The expanded Revised/W20 Renown chart has a Renown penalty for Auspice inappropriate behavior, and a few things that are similar for Breed and Tribe (though not quite so broad).<br /> <br /> I personally never use it, because if a player is after a Gift, it rarely is a Gift that doesn't make sense. If the pack is follow a Totem of a specific type, it makes sense to seek out Gifts that support the Totem's focus. If you're in a war pack, picking up a few out-of-splat Gifts that focus on fighting is hard to view as inappropriate. Sept is also something that can impact this. If a specific Tribe/small selection of Tribes dominate the Sept, being the odd one out without certain Gifts can be seen as a problem vis-a-vis lack of conformity, as well the Sept as a Caern Totem that sets goals and tone.<br /> <br /> Sometimes there's just plain old out-of-character things. There's a Revised Bone Gnawer Gift that I really like, but it's a &quot;meta-Gift&quot; that only works by expanding the function of three specific other Gifts; which aren't Gnawer specific Gifts. So letting people buy up the Gifts boosted even if out-of-splat is a bit necessary if you're going to let them have that Gift in the first place.<br /> <br /> If I want to push back, I focus on the process of getting the Gift. Have either the elders summoning spirits to instruct, or the spirits themselves, demand higher chiminage and justification for Gifts that are out-of-splat. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:22:48-07:00","id":954114,"title":"","content":"All Gifts are Kitsune Gifts. All Gifts. Some are Bastet GIfts too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T20:00:09-07:00","id":954160,"title":"","content":"I'd agree that Mothers touch could be worthwhile for any garou, meaning the difference between life and death..<br /> <br /> I'd disagree with a renown penalty unless it got really out of hand though.<br /> <br /> an Elder, of any auspice, might have reasons to want to be able to summon and command spirits. as part of an information net.<br /> <br /> Talens are often used almost as currency amongst the Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T20:32:55-07:00","id":954176,"title":"","content":"Heck, any level one through three Gift is a Hengeyokai Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:18:45-07:00","id":954610,"title":"","content":"For me, doing it once, is just frowned on by elders. Doing it too often (3 or more times) then leads to renown loss (temp points) for stepping out of one's auspice/tribe..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:02:58-07:00","id":954637,"title":"","content":"I don't do the negative Renown for Gifts not in your role. I just make them really hard to get. You have to CONFENCE. A out of tribe Garou to teach you. Spirits always ask for something very difficult. If a players the Gift it could take a few sessions just to earn the right to learn it. And if the Pack thinks it is a waste of time and resources....more flavor to the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:29:04-07:00","id":954675,"title":"","content":"Hmmn have wondered, think that the potential for misuse of a gift, will be considered before it is taught<br /> <br /> like a Child of Gaia might be quick enouugh to teach a Get of Fenris Ahroun who knows that he doesnt have tight enough hold of his Rage Mercy Who seeks to limit the possiblety of killing people in his tantrums<br /> <br /> but might be very leery of teaching it to a Shadow Lord Judge of doom Who wishes to bring people in alive, so he may &quot;Try&quot; them, for assorted crimes against the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> Anything curse of Lycanon can be used for the Red Talons would disapprove of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:33:10-07:00","id":954698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=954610#post954610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, doing it once, is just frowned on by elders. Doing it too often (3 or more times) then leads to renown loss (temp points) for stepping out of one's auspice/tribe..</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't like this sort of thing because it puts system over story without a solid reason as to why that might make the game more fun.<br /> <br /> If you have a Philodox that's the alpha of a War pack, there's a few Ahroun Gifts that are designed for the &quot;leader&quot; role over the &quot;warrior&quot; role. Why should the Philodox get punished for snagging those, when they're doing their job (even if it isn't the sole job of of their Auspice)?<br /> <br /> If you don't have all five Auspices in a pack, why would you penalize the characters that move to fill in the gaps the pack is missing? I once has a Ragabash in a pack with a Galliard and a Ahroun. My Ragabash ended up taking up a lot of the &quot;Theurge&quot; roles in the group, while the Galliard ended up taking up the &quot;Philodox&quot; roles in the pack. Again, where's the point in the Elder's convincing everyone to see the pack as being screw ups for doing their best with their numbers when my PC went after Spirit Speech, and the Galliard wanted Truth of Gaia?<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Plopping artificial limits doesn't really do much besides leading you to make exceptions to those limits when it turns out they don't make sense in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:39:57-07:00","id":954703,"title":"","content":"I personally don't mind people learning out of Auspice or Tribe Gifts as long as they're willing to do extra legwork to get them. Especially if the pack is lacking in an Auspice or 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T06:54:11-07:00","id":954928,"title":"","content":"Honestly if anything its the person Teaching who should or should not take the renown hit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:25:24-07:00","id":955034,"title":"","content":"In terms of Garou society, the question is are they properly fulfilling their auspice role and acting like home a member of the tribe should? If so, there is not social pressure in regard to out of scope Gifts. If however, the Ahroun doesn't seem to want to be an Ahroun and wants to act more like a Philodox by getting Philodox gifts and neglecting his Ahroun role, then there could be social pressure involved. But ultimately that is about not acting like they should for their auspice, not that they are learning out of auspice Gifts by themselves.<br /> <br /> The real issue with out of tribe, auspice, or breed gifts is everything that is needed to learn them. You need to find spirits willing to teach you, then convince them to do so (the character is worthy of it based on their past roleplay), then pay a lot more chiminage (and XP of course). It is much more of a hassle than the ones available to you naturally. Or at least should be.<br /> <br /> However, based on their pack totem, I do make certain Gifts more available to them as an ST. If they have Stag as their pack totem, then some of the Fianna gifts come into play (especially those not unique to the Fianna but found in other lists), and their pack totem can assist them with a lot of the Roleplay work although chiminage and XP costs ares till higher. For those totems that aren't Incarna who have tribes, it'll mean some extra work (for example if the PCs have Boar as their pack totem), but I can cobble together a list of Gifts that would make sense. Boar would have Stamina and Fighting feats, plus things related to eating and Grondr role inspired gifts. Raven would have a lot of Ragabash style gifts, and I'd look at some Silver Fang (Falcon) and Silent Strider (Owl) Gifts to see if anything fits generically with birds and flight.<br /> <br /> If the Players do not have one of each auspice, I am sympathetic to them trying to cover major holes in the Pack's abilities (if there is no Theurge, then someone probably is going to learn Spirit Speech). In character, the NPCs likely tell them just to recruit a new member from somewhere else, but the real issue is that there is not a player available so that this NPC grumbling isn't going to be anything more than flavor. Still, their major emphasis should still be their actual auspice, not any &quot;back up auspice&quot; role they are trying to fill.<br /> <br /> Out of breed gifts are probably the most difficult to learn, at least those not found on other lists. The key here, I think, is Ancestors. A Red Talon lupus is going to find it very heard to learn Master of Fire (and this would probably be one of the few times that roleplaying NPCs could involve real impact on relationships or renown - I imagine homid breed Gifts would be taboo for the Red Talons, but less so for other tribes) simply because there are no homid Ancestors for them. Silent Striders, Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers will have problems since Ancestors are restricted. However, given people's ancestral lineages can go back thousands and thousands of years, most Garou can probably find an ancestor of either homid or lupus breed somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:41:32-07:00","id":955097,"title":"","content":"You can learn gifts from other shifters directly. I generally consider that the only real method of getting out of tribe/breed/auspice gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:47:13-07:00","id":955151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=954928#post954928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly if anything its the person Teaching who should or should not take the renown hit.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955097#post955097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can learn gifts from other shifters directly. I generally consider that the only real method of getting out of tribe/breed/auspice gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's zero basis for this in the books though. If you had to learn out-of-splat Gifts directly from other Garou, it would be something worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> There's also numerous places the books make it clear that there are spirits that will teach anyone that can meet specific criteria (such as besting them in combat, which you don't have to be an Ahroun to do).<br /> <br /> I honestly don't get where the drive to be restrictive about this stuff comes from. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:10:20-07:00","id":955167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955151#post955151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> There's zero basis for this in the books though. If you had to learn out-of-splat Gifts directly from other Garou, it would be something worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> There's also numerous places the books make it clear that there are spirits that will teach anyone that can meet specific criteria (such as besting them in combat, which you don't have to be an Ahroun to do).<br /> <br /> I honestly don't get where the drive to be restrictive about this stuff comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The game presents learning from another CB as in all ways harder than going to a spirit. So why would anyone ever do this? I presumed that was how you got Gifts from Spirits you don't already have a relationship with(Tribe, Auspice, Breed) with some leeway for more common Gifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually this is a bigger question, how do CB know what gifts they can learn? How do they know who to Summon and why? Is that part of their training? Indoctination into a tribe etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:58:58-07:00","id":955208,"title":"","content":"As an aside, before W20 Mokole could learn gifts via mnesis, post W20 only the Mokole-mbembe can learn gifts from other Changing breeds via Mnesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:49:01-07:00","id":955326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955167#post955167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The game presents learning from another CB as in all ways harder than going to a spirit. So why would anyone ever do this? I presumed that was how you got Gifts from Spirits you don't already have a relationship with(Tribe, Auspice, Breed) with some leeway for more common Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've usually handled this by needing a sponsor or 2 of the appropriate breed/auspice/tribe who is on good standing with the spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually this is a bigger question, how do CB know what gifts they can learn? How do they know who to Summon and why? Is that part of their training? Indoctination into a tribe etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easiest solution I've found is to just roll out into the Rituals knowledge. Every dot in the knowledge covers knowing about that rank of gifts. <br /> If you want to make it a bit more difficult, you could even just cover just that person's breed/auspice/tribe gifts. So, need to know what philodox gifts are available for rank 3? Go ask a philodox that has Rituals 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:53:14-07:00","id":955351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955167#post955167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game presents learning from another CB as in all ways harder than going to a spirit. So why would anyone ever do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you don't always have access to the right spirits, or you don't want to do things &quot;above board&quot; for various reasons (ex: the Bringers of Light or the Grey Raptors are both Tribal camps that do a lot of things in secret and might consider teaching each other directly better than sending their members to outsiders to learn questionable Gifts; the difficulty of such learning might also be considered proof of the younger members' dedication to the Camp). This has always been presented as a back up option for special circumstances; not a default.<br /> <br /> There's also groups like Ronin and the fringes of Gnawer society that operate away from Septs and Tribes, leaving them with less access to traditional spirit-based learning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I presumed that was how you got Gifts from Spirits you don't already have a relationship with(Tribe, Auspice, Breed) with some leeway for more common Gifts. </div> </div> </div>What spirits teach Gifts pretty much has nothing to do with splats. Owl spirits teach Gifts all over the place (including in lists that are non-Strider Tribe lists). If the spirits that teach individual Gifts were more closely aligned with their linked splats? Ok, this would make sense. As it is, things are a giant mess and there's no consistent way to say, &quot;Oh, yeah, spider spirits were totally cool with teaching you this Theurge Gift cause you're a Theurge, but not this Glasswalker Gift because you're not a Glasswalker,&quot; if you're already on good terms with spider spirits.<br /> <br /> Your access to spirits comes for numerous sources besides splat. I've already mentioned things like Sept and Pack as being sources of in-roads with other kinds of spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually this is a bigger question, how do CB know what gifts they can learn? How do they know who to Summon and why? Is that part of their training? Indoctination into a tribe etc? </div> </div> </div>Personal experience with other shifters. Occult and Rituals if you feel like giving it a Knowledge roll. Lores if you like those. Otherwise... the books don't really consider this worth thinking too hard about.<br /> <br /> You can also just look at this from a more simple perspective. A Garou is looking for a Gift to aid them in doing X, so they ask for the help of a spirit that they think has the appropriate symbolism (I want to help keep people calm, so I'm going to Dove), and the spirit &quot;decides&quot; the Gift to learn, even though the player is selecting a more specific Gift out-of-character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:03:02-07:00","id":955375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=954698#post954698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really don't like this sort of thing because it puts system over story without a solid reason as to why that might make the game more fun.<br /> <br /> If you have a Philodox that's the alpha of a War pack, there's a few Ahroun Gifts that are designed for the &quot;leader&quot; role over the &quot;warrior&quot; role. Why should the Philodox get punished for snagging those, when they're doing their job (even if it isn't the sole job of of their Auspice)?<br /> <br /> If you don't have all five Auspices in a pack, why would you penalize the characters that move to fill in the gaps the pack is missing? I once has a Ragabash in a pack with a Galliard and a Ahroun. My Ragabash ended up taking up a lot of the &quot;Theurge&quot; roles in the group, while the Galliard ended up taking up the &quot;Philodox&quot; roles in the pack. Again, where's the point in the Elder's convincing everyone to see the pack as being screw ups for doing their best with their numbers when my PC went after Spirit Speech, and the Galliard wanted Truth of Gaia?<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> Plopping artificial limits doesn't really do much besides leading you to make exceptions to those limits when it turns out they don't make sense in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of rules like that already existing though.. And part of MY love for werewolf is cause there are clearly defined &quot;roles&quot;, much like 1e/2e ADND had clearly defined roles/powers for each class.. <br /> <br /> As for 'too small of a pack, so some have to step out of role to fill in those spots'.. for me i have not had a group size to where that actually happened.. YET.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if you look, there are many gifts that DO cross over multiple auspices/breeds/tribes.. To be honest i would actually like to see if someone's already done the leg work to make said chart up.. Write up all gifts, on the left of the chart, the right has a column for each auspice, breed and tribe, to see which are TRULY only in one group..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T22:25:15-07:00","id":955438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955375#post955375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are plenty of rules like that already existing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which rules penalize your Renown for spending XP after putting in IC effort to get something automatically as opposed to leveling Renown a ST call?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And part of MY love for werewolf is cause there are clearly defined &quot;roles&quot;, much like 1e/2e ADND had clearly defined roles/powers for each class. </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty weak point when you combine Auspice, Tribe, and Totem. There's also things like all Garou are supposed to participate in some of those rules with specific Auspices being specialists. All Garou are warriors. The Ahrouns are supposed to be the best of the best when it comes to waging war (mostly as individual skill but also as war leaders).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for 'too small of a pack, so some have to step out of role to fill in those spots'.. for me i have not had a group size to where that actually happened.. </div> </div> </div>Ok. I have. Multiple times. Saying, &quot;this hasn't happened to me,&quot; doesn't negate the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, if you look, there are many gifts that DO cross over multiple auspices/breeds/tribes.. To be honest i would actually like to see if someone's already done the leg work to make said chart up.. Write up all gifts, on the left of the chart, the right has a column for each auspice, breed and tribe, to see which are TRULY only in one group.. </div> </div> </div>I can do more of this if you really want, but I'm not that interested in doing a whole database just for this thread.<br /> <br /> I looked over my stuff of just the Rank 1 Gifts (there's 160 entries including a few where the Gift is renamed for different groups). Here's some details:<br /> <br /> 133/160 are just on one list. That's a solid 83% majority.<br /> 6/27 ones on multiple lists are only there because they are on one of the three extinct Tribal lists (so they're something + Bunyip/Croatoan/White Howler).<br /> 2/27 which don't overlap with the above point, are only there because a Camp Gift list.<br /> 10/27 including the above two points are on 3+ lists.<br /> 7/27 are the most common overlap of one Auspice list and one Tribe list.<br /> This includes a Bunyip Gift that's Rank 1 for Bunyip, and Rank 2 for all other Tribes... so that's a thing.<br /> <br /> There are a few common, core book, Gifts with a lot of overlap (Sense Wyrm and Mother's Touch are two examples) that might skew this as being more common than it is, but &quot;truly&quot; in one group is the clear default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T00:15:18-07:00","id":955461,"title":"","content":"To address the fluff side of the renown hit, the garou are VERY tribal and tribal pride. For all everyone likes to rant about progressive world of darkness and non racial blah blah blah the garou are pretty damned racist against each other. In ways that would make most humans pretty proud too might I add. Just because the swords of heimdall are gone doesn't mean all the fenrir prejudice against everyone else went away. Just the FAR RIGHT variant did. And it's the same in all tribes. Going to a different tribe and learning their customs may well seem like being a tribal traitor. <br /> <br /> Exceptions ofcourse being among the more free form tribes, gnawers and children of gaia come to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T00:24:02-07:00","id":955464,"title":"","content":"Gifts are something a spirit bestows on a garou. Axis Mundi has a longer paragraph about the gift learning process. So, if a character petitions a spirit successfully this is usually an accomplishment, and not a deed to be frowned upon. That also is true because a lot of gift choices don't make sense. 1st level 'Resist Pain', 2nd level soak gift, 3rd level damage boost - both true for the martial Get of Fenris, and the peace loving children of gaia - leaving the martial Bone Gnawer ahroun just asking &quot;What the hell?&quot;<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms said, players rarely go after gifts that are completely out-of-character.<br /> <br /> There are some gifts, that I consider archetypical for a tribe. &quot;Clap of Thunder&quot; or example. If another garou would learn that gift, the Shadow Lords might just find a way to kill him. Accident during a challenge. Volunteering for a suicide mission. 100 Scorpions in the bed (don't travel to Dorne).<br /> <br /> But besides that I rarely have NPC repercussions, or renown issues with gifts. The spirits will make it harder for a garou to proof to the spirit that he is worthy, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T00:26:38-07:00","id":955466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955461#post955461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address the fluff side of the renown hit, the garou are VERY tribal and tribal pride.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so I thought. But then OPP wrote in a book, that a sept can be a Glass Walker sept, even if no Glass Walker is living there, just because the other garou there are so very tribal, that they hold up Glass Walker customs anyway. Argh!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T00:50:19-07:00","id":955469,"title":"","content":"The Garou might be very Tribalist and all, but there are logical conclusions they have to embrace anyway.<br /> <br /> If an avatar spirit of Grandfather Thunder decides to teach a non-Shadow Lord a Gift that's only taught by Grandfather Thunder's brood? The Shadow Lords are not going to say, &quot;Fuck our Tribal Totem's judgement, screw that ass that 'stole' our Gift!&quot; They might have something to say about a non-Shadow Lord that didn't &quot;earn it&quot; in their eyes (such as calling in a favor with a high level Theurge to summon such a spirit and compel it to teach the Gift despite it's normal inclinations), but this is one of the reasons I've been pretty adamant against any default &quot;rule&quot; for these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T07:09:01-07:00","id":955556,"title":"","content":"It's important to note that the primary reason to learn out-of-BAT Gifts is to make up for a hole in the Pack. My Fostern Shadowlord Galliard had Sense Wyrm, Scent of the True Form, and Truth of Gaia. He spent most of his life in a Pack of 2 with his Coggie Ragabash buddy, so other than Gaia's Touch, they had a serious lack of Theurge/Philodox power.<br /> <br /> My Adren Get of Fenris Ragabash has twice as many Gifts, <i>none</i> of which are out-of-BAT because he's spent most of his game-life in a Pack with a Bone Gnawer Galliard, a Coggie Theurge and a Fianna Philodox. So the only Auspice we were missing was Ahroun, which is largely covered by our Tribal Gifts and lots of points in Skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:40:21-07:00","id":955901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955438#post955438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which rules penalize your Renown for spending XP after putting in IC effort to get something automatically as opposed to leveling Renown a ST call?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have to look, but i do remember seeing some.. though i MIGHT be getting game systems mixed up.. I will give you that much..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/954094-taking-out-of-tribe-gifts?p=955438#post955438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked over my stuff of just the Rank 1 Gifts (there's 160 entries including a few where the Gift is renamed for different groups). Here's some details:<br /> <br /> 133/160 are just on one list. That's a solid 83% majority.<br /> 6/27 ones on multiple lists are only there because they are on one of the three extinct Tribal lists (so they're something + Bunyip/Croatoan/White Howler).<br /> 2/27 which don't overlap with the above point, are only there because a Camp Gift list.<br /> 10/27 including the above two points are on 3+ lists.<br /> 7/27 are the most common overlap of one Auspice list and one Tribe list.<br /> This includes a Bunyip Gift that's Rank 1 for Bunyip, and Rank 2 for all other Tribes... so that's a thing.<br /> <br /> There are a few common, core book, Gifts with a lot of overlap (Sense Wyrm and Mother's Touch are two examples) that might skew this as being more common than it is, but &quot;truly&quot; in one group is the clear default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow.. 160?!! Didn't know there were THAT many..<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:57:40-07:00","id":955990,"title":"","content":"There's actually more than that. That's just Revised and W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T01:47:29-07:00","id":956209,"title":"","content":"However, you probably didn't account for gifts that are kind of similar, but have different names and mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T02:55:26-07:00","id":956228,"title":"","content":"True. But that gets very hard to do after a point. How similar is similar enough to get put together? There's no real objective metric I can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:31:51-07:00","id":961903,"title":"","content":"Things to keep in mind:<br /> 1) Tribe used to mean A LOT back in 1st and 2nd edition. The tribes weren't &quot;the Chess Team and the Football Team from the same High School&quot; like it's presented nowadays... the tribes were North Korea, Libya, France, Columbia, etc... if you got caught sleeping with each other's kinfolk, trespassing in each other's territory, or trying to steal each other's secrets (or in ownership of them afterward) there was outright murder to pay. Much like the Floppy Disk icon, we just all accept it means 'Save' these days despite half the world's computer users having never seen a disk in their lives, many of us still carry around vestigial canon in our heads that's not really been reprinted since.<br /> <br /> 2) Tribe STILL means a lot. Tribe is more than just some habits and lineage. There's a reason you can't round up some scottish garou and reform the White Howlers. Tribal gifts involve ancient pacts, loyalties to totems, and kinship with spiritual broods. Knowing the list of Fenrir gifts, what teaches each, and going out to ask a bear spirit to teach it to you isn't something you can do at your local library. Bear and her brood didn't make that deal with France... she made that deal with Libya. So even if you somehow knew the deal existed, asking about it is a borderline international incident and sure as hell a grave party foul.<br /> <br /> 3) Out-of-Breed and Out-of-Auspice are very different from Out-of-Tribe (for 'See the Above' reasons), and given the trends in overall theme and attitude in subsequent editions of Werewolf, these two are probably barely an issue in Garou society nowadays compared to in the past... but Spirits aren't that malleable. You probably still need a in-Breed/Auspice reference with you when you summon the spirit, or learn it from another shifter directly, or have a silver tongue and a really good bribe. Because spirits aren't people... they don't deviate from natural order with anything resembling ease. Their minds simply don't work that way, unless you're dealing with a more powerful Jaggling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:22:14-07:00","id":961928,"title":"","content":"The problem with all that...is that it really doesn't match up with the text.<br /> <br /> The Tribal Gift lists are not presented as &quot;secrets&quot; that Tribes would kill over. They're not presented as the results of ancient pacts with spirit broods (which gets really hard to claim when you have things like, &quot;Any Gaian spirit can teach this Gift,&quot; as a thing). The books don't actually present a single specific in-character reason why out-of-splat Gifts should be harder to get than in-splat Gifts.<br /> <br /> I personally think that it's a flaw in the game (the Gift Lists and what kind of spirits teach them are kind of ridiculously all over the place), but it really doesn't hold that any attempt to restrict access to out-of-splat Gifts as any more than personal play style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T15:53:17-07:00","id":961939,"title":"","content":"&quot;In accordance with sacred pacts made at the dawn of time, spirits grant mystical blessings and powers...&quot; &quot;Different tribes, auspices and even breeds are the inheritors of different mystical legacies, and so the Gifts normally granted to them differ.&quot; That is literally the first paragraph under &quot;Gifts&quot; in W20, pg 155. <br /> <br /> &quot;Some Garou are extremely touchy about outsiders learning their tribal blessings, while others believe the practice strengthens the Garou Nation as a whole in its war against the Wyrm&quot; W20 pg 172. (Keep in mind... over the course from 1st edition to W20 the shifters and tribes went from virtually at war with one another to the Superfriends, so this is as nice as any publication has presented the idea.)<br /> <br /> &quot;Different tribes, auspices, and even breeds learn different gifts. Each group has its own secret and its own unique spiritual connections.&quot; WtA Revised, first paragraph under Gifts, pg 132.<br /> <br /> &quot;Learning a Gift from another tribe requires the Garou to be on good terms with a member of that tribe (usually a packmate) who can summon the appropriate spirit. Even then, the Garou must convince the spirit that the Gift will be put to good use - and not used against any members of the spirit's patron tribe.&quot; WtA Revised, 143<br /> <br /> That's the first minute or two of looking. I could find more, but that seems like sufficient effort at this point. This has always been the narrative as to why Gifts have divisions. Technically there is NOTHING stopping a Cub from learning a Rank 5 gift other than the fact that it just will never happen. Ever.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}